  "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#semiotic_projection_1",
  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the textual material expressing Trump's internal monologue",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the textual material 'you can't lose in 2020 if there is no 2020.' This text represents the internal thought process of Donald Trump as depicted in the meme. The user is invited to imagine themselves in the position of the meme's subject, contemplating this cynical political strategy. The projection is onto the textual material because the meme's humor and critique hinge on the user internalizing and evaluating this absurd proposition, which is presented as Trump's thinking. The visual material (Donald_Trump) supports this projection by showing his smug expression, which reinforces the idea that the user is being asked to identify with or imagine the perspective of the person who holds this thought.",
  "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface",
